# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on win-64 and linux-64, and core.autocrlf=true on
# Windows converts text files to CRLF on checkout. That is fine for files
# people edit, but not for one a tool rewrites in place: pixi writes
# pixi.lock with LF on every platform, so after any `pixi install` the
# working tree held LF where Git expected CRLF and reported the lockfile as
# modified with zero changed lines. A phantom diff trains you to stop
# reading `git status`, which is worse than the cosmetic problem it looks
# like.
#
# Scoped to pixi.lock deliberately. Other generated files here are written
# through Python's text mode, which already produces CRLF on Windows, so
# they round-trip correctly and pinning them would force a needless rewrite.

pixi.lock text eol=lf

# Everything else: let Git detect text and apply the platform default.
* text=auto
